        "body": "Write the decision in one sentence so the reviewer knows what would count as an answer. Use the same definition across the queue and the review so the counts agree. Name the person who can close the question and the date by which the answer is needed. The separation checklist coverage record should let a second reviewer rebuild the decision from employee record and access removal. For the outsourced HR queue, the separation checklist coverage record is matched to the employee file and dated by the named HR owner before the case is closed.\n\nA clean-looking status is not evidence that the underlying work is correct. Separate the request from the decision, because a complete request is not an approval. Note the observation window; a case without a period cannot be compared later. The separation checklist coverage case note should show what the HR record held at the time and who reviewed it. The separation checklist coverage note stays in the HR service folder, where a second reviewer confirms it against the approved policy before the weekly audit.\n\nState explicitly what is in scope and what is out of scope for the case. Do not let a deadline expand a role beyond its written limit. If the team cannot reproduce the result from the record, the control is not finished. In the separation checklist coverage queue, an item without a next action is treated as an exception. At the monthly HR review, the separation checklist coverage item is re-read and any change is recorded in the same employee file."
